+  // WI-5863: surface the DHT signalling outcome onto the returned encryptedSocket
+  // (the object hyperswarm hands back to app code as the 'connection' socket) —
+  // these three were destructured above but only ever lived on the internal `c`
+  // state machine, so app code could never distinguish "punch believed to have
+  // succeeded but the data path is dead" (relayed:false) from "the relay path
